  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0225 and it contains four tables: Company, User, Request_Log, and User_Feedback. The Company table has the following columns: Authorization_Token, Company_ID (primary key), Company_Name, Creation_Time, Modification_Time, and Token_Hash_Value. The User table has the following columns: Company_ID (foreign key referencing Company), Creation_Time, Modification_Time, Password_Hash_Value, Password_Salt_Value, Permission_Level, User_ID (primary key), and User_Name. The Request_Log table has the following columns: Compression_Result, Probe_Information, Request_Data, Request_ID (primary key), Status, Timestamp, and User_ID (foreign key referencing User). The User_Feedback table has the following columns: Comment, Creation_Time, Feedback_ID (primary key), Rating, and User_ID (foreign key referencing User). The primary keys for each table are indicated in parentheses. Foreign keys are indicated with the name of the table they reference. The User_ID column in the User table and the Request_ID column in the Request_Log table are foreign keys referencing the User_ID column in the User table and the User_ID column in the User_Feedback table, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "Design and implement a database management system for an enterprise-level natural language processing (NLP) platform, which shall support:\n\nCompany management (store basic company information, authorization tokens and their hash values, record creation and modification timestamps),      \n\nUser management (store detailed user information, password salt values and their hash values, manage permissions and record creation and modification timestamps),\n\nRequest processing log recording (store request ID, user ID, status, timestamp, request data, compression results and probe information),\n\nand User feedback management (store rating, comments and creation timestamp).",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0225.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0225\nCREATE TABLE `company` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `modification_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `authorization_token` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `token_hash_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `modification_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_hash_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password_salt_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `permission_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `company` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `request_log` (\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `request_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `compression_result` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `probe_information` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`request_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `request_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_feedback` (\n  `feedback_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`feedback_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_feedback_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
